NeoSCAD patch to manifold-rust 0.15.0 (crates.io): the ear clipper keeps a
bounding box for each outer ring (grown as holes are joined in), and the
two bridge searches (cut_keyhole, find_closer_bridge) skip a ring whose
box shows that none of its verts can pass the search's tests. Before,
every hole walked every outer ring, which is quadratic: 200 lines of
extruded text (30,000 rings) spent over 90% of 34 s there. Output is
unchanged: each skipped ring is one the walk could not have taken a
connector from, with margins well above rounding. The `ccw` part of the
test is used only at scales where `ccw` itself cannot underflow or
overflow (distances and epsilon at most 1e75, margin at least 1e-150);
outside them the ring is walked. Tests: crates/geom/tests/kernel_patches.rs,
and the crate's own (src/polygon_earclip_tests.rs: a grid of glyphs, and
a bridge `ccw` finds through underflow and through overflow).

Upstream: proposed as branch `neoscad/earclip-ring-boxes`
(commit 1ff6373, larsbrubaker/manifold-rust#9) of a fork of
larsbrubaker/manifold-rust, on top of `neoscad/earclip-loop-visitor`
(0001), on its `main` at 9989b92 (0.15.0 plus two QuickHull commits and a regression
test for unions, which touch none of these files). This patch is that commit's changes under src/,
byte for byte apart from CRLF line endings.

Apply from the crate root on top of 0001: patch -p1 < this file.
The crate's older sources use CRLF line endings; files this series
adds use LF.
See vendor/README.md ("The keyhole ring-box patch").

